<section class='page-hero'>
  <div class='wrap'>
    <div class='page-hero__eyebrow'>Legal</div>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class='page-hero__sub'>Last updated April 29, 2026</p>
  </div>
</section>
<article class='legal-body'>
  <p>
    Once Upon A Time, Inc. ("OUAT", "we", "us") is a 501(c)(3) nonprofit serving children and families in Queens, NY.
    This policy explains what information we collect from visitors and program participants, how we use it, and the
    choices you have.
  </p>
  <h2>Information we collect</h2>
  <h3>Account information</h3>
  <p>
    When you create an account or enroll a child in a program, we collect name, email, phone, billing address, and child
    profile details (name, age, allergies, special conditions, emergency contact). Payment is processed by our
    PCI-compliant payment processor; we do not store full card numbers.
  </p>
  <h3>Usage information</h3>
  <p>
    We use first-party analytics to understand site usage. We do not sell or share personal information with third-party
    advertisers.
  </p>
  <h2>How we use it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To provide programs, classes, and donor services you've requested</li>
    <li>To send transactional emails (receipts, class reminders, password resets)</li>
    <li>To send program updates and our newsletter — you may unsubscribe at any time</li>
    <li>To meet legal and tax-reporting obligations as a registered nonprofit</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You may request a copy of, correction of, or deletion of your personal data at any time by emailing
    <a href='mailto:contact@onceuponatime.org'>contact@onceuponatime.org</a>. California, EU, and similar jurisdictions
    have additional rights under applicable law; we honor those requests.
  </p>
  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    We use a small number of essential cookies (session, language, accessibility) and an optional analytics cookie. You
    can opt out at any time via the cookie banner or by clearing your browser cookies.
  </p>
  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    Programs are designed for children, but accounts are held by parents or legal guardians. We do not knowingly collect
    personal information directly from children under 13 outside of the parent/guardian flow.
  </p>
  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions? Reach our privacy lead at <a href='mailto:contact@onceuponatime.org'>contact@onceuponatime.org</a> or
    87-61 111th St, Richmond Hill, NY 11418.
  </p>
</article>

